WEBVTT

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.110
out of that wreck and destroy them.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.130
Quick.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.260
You're hurt, Bradley.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.830
No, those armored cars are built for protection.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:39.870
Good.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.510
They'll take the bullets in the armored car and keep them until the corps order to impound them comes through.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.800
tell him to take it easy. If the Hornet discovers

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.900
he's sending munitions out of the country, we'll have

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.020
the G-Men on us, as well as the police and the Hornet.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:51.120
Better get Max on the phone. Yes?

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.670
Max Gregory speaking. All right, put him up.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.660
Here. Gregory, you better get that last

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.920
shipment of munitions off your hands.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.820
at once. Young Roberts is making things difficult. I was about to go and see him. Perhaps you

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:11.680
could suggest some way of putting on pressure. I'll take care of it. He's got a warehouse

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:17.110
at 39th and Grove, hasn't he? With the new mayor in office, we got the hoodlums on the

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:23.840
run. Maybe now he can take a little time off and run down the Green Hornet. That's a pretty

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.580
large order, isn't it, Michael? What do you want me to do, give you six months vacation

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.920
with pay or something? Six months, is it?

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.040
Give me six days and I'll run the Spalapine to earth.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.650
The same gang maybe started this fire.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:32.990
Very likely.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.560
You go in there and find out all you can about who did start that fire.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:37.960
I'm going to John's office.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.040
Yes, this is John Roberts.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.360
You say you've got the fire under control?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:47.840
You don't know how it started.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:50.290
All right.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.940
I'll have the insurance people come down.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:52.540
Thanks.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.550
Rick Reed, gosh, am I glad to see you.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.410
Hello, John.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:05:59.930
I overheard your phone.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.540
conversation. So that fire did cause you

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.850
considerable damage. Yes. Of course, my

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.570
insurance will cover the actual loss,

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:09.790
but I'll lose a lot of important customers and

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:13.400
well... Spell it. That fire wasn't

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.530
accidental. Someone's trying to drive me in the

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:17.560
line, same as they did Charles. What's the

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.840
racket? Well, it's this way. I kept this

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.640
business right up to the standard that Charles set.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.000
As you know, we do a lot of shipping by rails

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.780
in carload lots. Well, the other day a fellow

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.860
came in and demanded that I allow him to ship

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:29.960
on...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.860
of my bill of lading.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.440
Wanted to commandeer my space.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:33.350
What do you mean?

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.250
Well, if I was sending two cars,

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.210
he'd take over one.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:37.900
Wouldn't tell me who he was

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:38.620
or what he was shipping,

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:39.400
but he made it clear

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.140
that I'd have trouble

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:40.840
if I refused.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.120
So that fire was the result

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:43.780
of your refusal?

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:44.900
I'm sure of it.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.040
Well, there's been a series

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.120
of smaller attacks,

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:48.390
breakdown of trucks,

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.470
attacks on my drivers.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:50.770
Have you notified the police?

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:51.740
No.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.260
You remember what happened

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.560
to Charles when he went

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:55.140
to the police.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.700
Very well done, Dean.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.010
This fire will bring young Mr. Roberts to terms.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.940
I have one more little surprise for him.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:05.880
Down at the harbor.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:06.970
Tell him to talk, Turkey.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:07.710
Very good.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.360
I'll talk again to Roberts tomorrow.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:09.820
Better not.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:11.020
He knows you now.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:11.740
He might bring something.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:12.660
Let me handle it.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:13.460
All right.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:19.330
All right, John.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.390
You talk to him out here.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.800
Put Jenks in the other room so he can hear what he has to say.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:24.820
I sure appreciate this, Britt.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.430
Well, we've got to rid this city and those crooks.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:28.240
See you later.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:29.450
So long, Frank.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:34.180
He's on his way up now.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.100
Better get inside.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:43.980
What can I do for you?

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:49.180
That's right.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.160
What do you want?

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.200
Listen, buddy, you can save yourself a lot of trouble.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.300
We made your proposition, which you refused.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.840
But in view of what happened since, maybe you've changed your mind.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:07:59.970
You mean that you and your...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.820
The crowd are responsible for that warehouse fire?

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:02.500
Never mind, then.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.040
I'm giving you one last chance to come in with this unconditionally.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:09.240
Yes, but I've got to know what your name is and what you propose to ship.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.560
You want to know too much.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.350
Look out for trouble.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:24.090
I think he suspected so.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:24.870
Okay, thanks.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.010
Sentinel reporter following me.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:03.620
Get him.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:10.630
Follow him, Kato.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:14.700
Hey.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.680
Hey, what is this, a stick-up?

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.360
Just another scoop for the Sentinel.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.950
And final negotiations with Robert are now on the way.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:29.890
If all goes well, shipment of arms will go.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.010
forward at once. That's all.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:36.820
Put it in code and get it off immediately.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.780
The client door, sir. That will be

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.380
in the report on Roberts. Let them in.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:55.360
What have you got here?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.480
No, ma'am. Roberts had him planted to try him.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.740
What did you bring him up here for?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.980
Well, no chance to get rid of him.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.860
and he knows too much to turn him loose.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:04.650
That means we've got to strike at that shipment of his tonight.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:05.690
Throw him in the closet.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.170
I'll have him taken care of later.

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:22.500
Clear water junction.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.300
You board the train.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.300
You'll get your final instructions from Monroe.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.320
Thanks for your cooperation.

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:45.200
The traffic bureau gave you the name of the owner of the car

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.700
that carried off Mr. Jenks?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:49.400
Yes, it was registered to a Max Gregory.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:54.920
The 311 Garden Building.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.220
Mr. Gregory's going to be asked some questions tonight.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.520
I have a green point.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:29.780
Says again.

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:38.530
The train in Robert's shipment will be boarded at Clearwater Junction at midnight tonight.

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:47.140
Robert's cars and everything behind him will be uncoupled on the long gray west of Summit.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.490
That's all. Put it into code.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:56.210
Never mind the code. Take as it is.

00:12:56.370 --> 00:12:57.190
The Green Hornet.

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:57.980
Give it to me.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:06.310
Glad to see you, Honor.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.680
We've decided we could make good use of you in our organization

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.080
if we can come to terms.

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:12.300
I'll dictate the terms.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:13.720
I'm taking over your organization.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:14.960
I know all about it.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.630
Green Hornet might need help

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:19.990
transporting secretly ammunition.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.310
Not from you, Gregory.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.890
All I want from you is the names of your associates.

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:25.060
All right.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.220
You have the upper hand.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.580
I guess I have no other choice.

00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:35.150
Why'd you ask for it?

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.240
Another one, eh? What's your connection with this gang?

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.330
I don't know about this. How can I map it? I'm a reporter from the Sentinel.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:12.750
The Sentinel, eh? That muck-breaking reform sheet.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.730
I suppose you're after the reward for the capture of the Hornet.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:19.010
Word or no reward, the Sentinel's out to get you and the rest of the crooks in this town.

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:22.050
If you keep me here, the rest of this gang's going out to wreck a train.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:25.180
And blame it on me, eh? Well, I'll take care of that.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.350
Phone the police. These men are wanted for munitions and gun running.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.570
And don't try to follow me.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:37.350
Two, a couple of robin's cars.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.420
Great, captured.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:31.580
You got me wrong.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:32.900
I'm just bumming a ride.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.900
Rain, go let her take the consequences.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:40.960
No, don't shoot.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.180
I'll talk.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:43.870
The others are up front.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:48.810
No, you don't.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:03.680
Thank you.
